:: Low Morale [event main_quest] {"position":"4700,500","size":"100,100"}
/* Quest "Morale" (main_morale), STAGE1_PROPOSAL.md 4.6. The gym contract is signed and the workload has doubled. I tell
   $mom.callName and $sister.callName to dress a little nicer and be friendlier with the staff (their rounds already exist as
   tasks). $darius.name pushes back, not morally but analytically: productivity peaks twenty minutes after $mom.callName walks
   through the room, and he'd like to know why. Since $sister.callName turned him down he watches the family more closely.
   The choice sets $flags.dariusBroughtIn:
     true   a half-truth ("it's a nudge, it's in the brochure"), a title and a small stake ($darius.equity): a Stage 2 ally
     false  shut out: he stays suspicious, and the log pull in The Crack 2 looks guilty
   A line changes with how the gym dinner went ($mom.flags.gymDinner). */
<<silent>><<SetBackground $locations[13].img>><</silent>>
<<if $mom.flags.gymDinner === true>>
$gymOwner.name signed the full contract the morning after his dinner with $mom.callName, eleven locations and a twelfth next spring, and sent a fruit basket the size of a car tire.
<<else>>
$gymOwner.name signed the morning after our dinner, with the discount I gave him and a handshake that went on for a while, eleven locations and a twelfth next spring.
<</if>> That was ten days ago. Since then the office has been running like a kitchen on a Saturday night.

Eleven gyms means eleven site surveys, eleven routers, eleven installations after closing time. $brian.name has been soldering emitter rings at his desk with his lunch balanced on his knee. $ethan.name hasn't told a joke since Tuesday, which is the most worrying number in the building. $darius.name has a spreadsheet for the spreadsheets. Nobody says anything about it, because nobody has the energy to.

The company Morale on my dashboard has been going down a little every day, a slow, steady slope, the kind you don't notice until you look at the whole week.

<<linkreplace "Do something about it">>
I call $mom.callName and $sister.callName into the meeting room at the same time, which I don't usually do. $sister.callName sits down next to $mom.callName and steals a mint from the bowl. $mom.callName takes the bowl away from her without looking.

<<silently>><<SetBackground $locations[15].img>><</silently>>

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "I'm guessing you've both noticed, but the team is running on fumes." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Honey, $brian.name fell asleep at his desk yesterday with the soldering iron still on, and $ethan.name had to go over and unplug it. I've been bringing him an extra sandwich every day since, because I don't think he eats when he gets like that." },
{ who: $sister, text: "And $ethan.name didn't even make a joke about it. I waited for one, and it never came, which honestly worried me more than the iron." },
{ who: $player, text: "So here's what I'd like. For the next few weeks, I want the two of you to be the best part of their day. Dress a little nicer, stay a bit longer at each desk, laugh at their jokes even when they're bad. Whatever you're already doing on your rounds, just do more of it." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

They look at each other. It's the first time I've given them the same order in the same room, and something passes between them that I can't quite read, some kind of polite curiosity. As far as I know, neither of them has any idea what the other one's rounds look like.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $sister, text: "Define nicer. Are we talking blazer nice, or the other kind?" },
{ who: $player, text: "The kind they'd notice. I'll leave the details to you two, you're both better at this than I am." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Oh, I can do that, I've got the blue dress, the one with the belt, and everybody always says something when I wear the blue dress." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Well, now I have to beat the blue dress, which is hardly fair, because the blue dress is a classic." },
{ who: $mom, text: "It's not a competition, sweetie." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Everything is a competition." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

Everybody laughs, because it's a joke. It's also the first time they've ever been put side by side for the same audience, and from the way $sister.callName glances at $mom.callName's legs when she stands up, I don't think it's entirely a joke anymore.

<<linkreplace "A few days later">>
<<silently>><<SetBackground $locations[14].img>><</silently>>
It works, and a lot faster than I expected.

The blue dress shows up on Tuesday. $sister.callName answers on Wednesday with a skirt I've never seen and a blouse that she has, technically, buttoned. The Morale line on my dashboard flattens out, and then on Thursday it starts to climb, a little at first, then a lot. $ethan.name tells a joke about the printer at a quarter past ten. $brian.name eats lunch at a table like a person. By Friday the office sounds the way it did before the gyms.

On Friday afternoon $darius.name knocks on the edge of my desk with a printout in his hand, and he doesn't look like he's here to chat.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $darius, text: "Do you have ten minutes? It concerns us rather than a client, I'm afraid." },
{ who: $player, text: "Sure. Sit down." },
{ text: "He doesn't sit. He lays the printout on my desk, squares it with the edge, and taps it with one finger." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

It's a chart of the last week: $ethan.name's commits, closed tickets, $brian.name's soldering log and $darius.name's own output, all on one timeline, and on top of it a row of small colored marks, some blue and some yellow. I have a bad feeling I know what they stand for before he says a word.

<<linkreplace "Hear him out">>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $darius, text: "I log everything. It's a habit I've never managed to break. Those marks represent every occasion on which one of them passed through the main room on her rounds." },
{ who: $darius, text: "Productivity peaks roughly twenty minutes after your $mom.relation walks through the room, and it does so every single time. Your $sister.relation's effect is smaller and concentrated almost entirely on $brian.name." },
{ who: $darius, text: "I'm not suggesting anything improper. People work better when someone is kind to them; that's well documented, and there's a respectable literature on it. But that effect is diffuse. It doesn't arrive twenty minutes later with this kind of regularity. What I'm looking at resembles a dose far more than it resembles morale." },
{ who: $player, text: "A dose. Okay. That's, uh, kind of a weird word for it." },
{ who: $darius, text: "Perhaps. I'd still like to understand why it looks like one." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

He isn't accusing me of anything. He's doing the most dangerous thing a smart person can do, which is being curious, out loud, in my office. And he's been watching them. Since $sister.callName turned him down, he's been watching my family a little more closely than before, and now he's found a pattern in it.

He's the first one to put any of it together, and while he doesn't have all of it, he has more than I'm comfortable with. My mouth has gone dry, and I'm very aware that he's waiting for me to say something.

<<linkreplace "Decide what to do with him">>
<div id="morale-choice" class="choices">
<div>
<<link "Bring him in with a half-truth">><<replace "#morale-choice">>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "Can you, uh, close the door for a second?" },
{ text: "He closes it and sits down for the first time." },
{ who: $player, text: "Okay, so, you basically found the Veil. Well, a low-power version of it. It's in the ventilation, and it's been running since we moved in. It's the same nudge we sell, honestly, the stuff that's in the brochure, calm and focus and a bit of warmth. And I guess when somebody walks through and makes people smile, the unit sort of... amplifies that? That's kind of what it's built to do. So what you're seeing is probably that." },
{ who: $darius, text: "In our own office, without telling anyone." },
{ who: $player, text: "I mean, where else was I supposed to test it? And if I'd told everyone, it's not really a pilot anymore, is it, it's a... placebo thing. Everybody would just feel whatever they expected to feel." },
{ text: "He thinks about that. I can see him turning it over, looking for the crack, and finding one, and deciding it's small enough to live with." },
{ who: $darius, text: "Strictly speaking, not telling people is a flaw in the study design as well, just a different one. Though I'll concede it's the more common one." },
{ who: $player, text: "Yeah, well, that's kind of why I need someone around who notices that stuff. How about Head of Analytics? An actual title, and a stake in the company, a small one, but a real one. And from now on you get the raw data, all of it, including ours." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

The raw data from the office vent is going to have to look like a low-power Veil, which means a week of late nights building him a history that holds up, and I'm already dreading it. Still, I'd rather have $darius.name inside the tent, where I can at least see what he's measuring.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $darius, text: "Including ours." },
{ who: $player, text: "Yeah. Everything." },
{ text: "He stands up, picks up his printout, and for the first time since he started here he offers me his hand like an equal." },
{ who: $darius, text: "Then I accept, gladly. And thank you for being straight with me. I suspect that wasn't an easy conversation to have." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

He means it, too. I wait until he's back at his desk before I let my shoulders down, and then I open a blank spreadsheet and start building him a history.

<<set $flags.dariusBroughtIn to true>>
<<set $darius.equity to 1>>
<<run State.variables.darius.stats.morale = Math.clamp(State.variables.darius.stats.morale + 15, State.variables.darius.stats.min.morale, State.variables.darius.stats.max.morale)>>
<<UpdateStat "+" "Morale" 4>>
<<UpdateStat "+" "Corruption" 1>>
<<NextQuest $player>>
<<ReturnFromEvent>>
<</replace>><</link>>
</div>
<div>
<<link "Shut him out">><<replace "#morale-choice">>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "Honestly? I think that's just good office culture, $darius.name. People like my family, they're likable people. I don't really know what else to tell you. Write a paper about it if you want." },
{ who: $darius, text: "That's certainly one explanation, although I'm not sure it accounts for the timing." },
{ who: $player, text: "Well, it's the one I've got." },
{ who: $darius, text: "With respect, culture doesn't usually arrive in twenty-minute doses." },
{ who: $player, text: "Look, I don't want to argue about this. Your contract runs through the end of the year, and what I need from you until then is the gyms, not charts about my family. Can we leave it there?" },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

There's a short pause. He doesn't argue. He picks up the printout, folds it once down the middle, and puts it in the inside pocket of his jacket instead of the bin.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $darius, text: "Understood. I'll focus on the gyms." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

He goes back to his desk. For the rest of the afternoon he works exactly as hard as always, and every time $mom.callName walks through the main room, he looks at his watch.

<<set $flags.dariusBroughtIn to false>>
<<run State.variables.darius.stats.morale = Math.clamp(State.variables.darius.stats.morale - 10, State.variables.darius.stats.min.morale, State.variables.darius.stats.max.morale)>>
<<UpdateStat "+" "Morale" 2>>
<<UpdateStat "+" "Corruption" 2>>
<<NextQuest $player>>
<<ReturnFromEvent>>
<</replace>><</link>>
</div>
</div>
<</linkreplace>>
<</linkreplace>>
<</linkreplace>>
<</linkreplace>>
